      "writtenOn": "2020-08-21T20:08:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have now tested with lock debugging enabled.\n\nIt does not need to be a separate lock, but the locking mechanism gets more complicated around the release path on a failed message if we have only 1. The device is held locked on that path, so if we use the same lock, every function on that path needs _locked variants, or we need to release the lock at the start of the drop handling and reacquire after, both of which are not great complexity-wise.",
